---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout 
  title="TypeScript Cheat Sheet | Free Types, Generics & Utility Types"
  description="Complete TypeScript cheat sheet with types, interfaces, generics, utility types, and common patterns. Free reference for TypeScript developers."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>TypeScript<br><span>Cheat Sheet</span></h1>
    <p>Types, interfaces, generics, utility types, and common patterns. From basics to advanced TypeScript.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Basic Types</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Primitives</h3>
        <pre><code>let x&#58; number = 42;
let s&#58; string = "hello";
let b&#58; boolean = true;
let n&#58; null = null;
let u&#58; undefined = undefined;
let sym&#58; symbol = Symbol();
let big&#58; bigint = 100n;</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Arrays &amp; Tuples</h3>
        <pre><code>let nums&#58; number[] = [1, 2, 3];
let strs&#58; Array&lt;string&gt; = ["a"];
let tuple&#58; [string, number] = ["a", 1];</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Interfaces &amp; Types</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Interfaces</h3>
        <pre><code>interface User &#123;
  name&#58; string;
  age&#58; number;
  email?&#58; string;  // optional
  readonly id&#58; number;
&#125;</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Type Aliases</h3>
        <pre><code>type ID = string | number;
type Point = &#123; x&#58; number; y&#58; number &#125;;
type Status = "active" | "inactive";</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Generics</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Generic Functions</h3>
        <pre><code>function identity&lt;T&gt;(arg&#58; T)&#58; T &#123;
  return arg;
&#125;
const num = identity&lt;number&gt;(42);
const str = identity("hello");</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Generic Constraints</h3>
        <pre><code>interface HasLength &#123;
  length&#58; number;
&#125;
function log&lt;T extends HasLength&gt;(arg&#58; T) &#123;
  console.log(arg.length);
&#125;</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Utility Types</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Common Utilities</h3>
        <pre><code>Partial&lt;User&gt;     // all optional
Required&lt;User&gt;     // all required
Pick&lt;User, "name"&gt; // subset
Omit&lt;User, "age"&gt;  // exclude
Readonly&lt;User&gt;     // immutable</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Type Guards</h3>
        <pre><code>function isString(v&#58; unknown)&#58; v is string &#123;
  return typeof v === "string";
&#125;
if (isString(val)) &#123;
  val.toUpperCase(); // narrowed
&#125;</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Classes</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Class Definition</h3>
        <pre><code>class Animal &#123;
  constructor(public name&#58; string) &#123;&#125;
  speak()&#58; string &#123;
    return `$&#123;this.name&#125; speaks`;
  &#125;
&#125;
const a = new Animal("Dog");</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Access Modifiers</h3>
        <pre><code>class Example &#123;
  public x&#58; number;    // everywhere
  protected y&#58; number; // class + subclass
  private z&#58; number;   // class only
&#125;</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Download</h2>
    <p>Print this page or save as PDF for quick reference.</p>
    <p><strong>Tip:</strong> Use Ctrl+P (Cmd+P on Mac) to print or save as PDF.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
